Alabama, Birmingham. Medical Properties Trust, Inc. was incorporated in 2003 in Maryland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Larry H. Portal | Senior VP & Senior Advisor to the CEO | Age 55 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 121 people. Revenue per employee of $8.0M ranks in the top quartile among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 15%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $213K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Medical Properties Trust, Inc. is a small-cap real estate business with a $983M market cap on $972M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -14% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 2% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 16.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 22.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 8.9% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (33.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Real Estate peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 86% leaves thin coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"amber","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 75/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Real Estate peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 36% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","20 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Medical Properties Trust (MPT) Returns To Profit, Is It 65% Below Fair Value?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nyse-mpt/medical-properties-trust/news/medical-properties-trust-mpt-returns-to-profit-is-it-65-belo","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794450289.773,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.863,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Head to Head Analysis: Medical Properties Trust (MPT) & Its Competitors","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/09/head-to-head-analysis-medical-prope